    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nI added a duplicate-telephone check to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **`EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone`** (new function) \u2014 reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` (whose telephone `ValidateOwnerFields` has already normalized to 10 digits), scans every existing owner via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throws `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` when a normalized telephone matches. It normalizes both sides (strips non-digits) so the comparison is robust.\n\n2. **`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`** (new checked exception) \u2014 extends `Exception` so it appears in the `throws` clause and is routed to an escalation handler.\n\n3. **`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneExceptionHandler`** (new escalation handler) \u2014 responds **409 Conflict**, mirroring the existing telephone-validation handler's body shape (`{\"errors\": [\"telephone\"]}`).\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `ensureUniqueTelephone` step between `validate` and `build`, under the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps. Placing it after `validate` means normalization happens first, and it runs before `build`/`save` so a duplicate never gets persisted.\n\nBoth new tests pass: `coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` (same telephone \u2192 409) and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` (distinct telephones \u2192 2xx).",
